menu "Lua runtime"

    choice CLU_LUA_VERSION
        prompt "Lua version"
        default CLU_LUA_5_3
        help
            Real CLU firmware embeds Lua 5.3, and OM.LUA / user scripts are written for it.
            Lua 5.5 is faster and leaner, but rejects scripts that use `global` as a name or
            assign to a for-loop variable, and has no bit32 library.

        config CLU_LUA_5_3
            bool "Lua 5.3.6 (same as real CLU)"
        config CLU_LUA_5_5
            bool "Lua 5.5.1 (experimental)"
    endchoice

    config CLU_LUA_MEM_LIMIT_KB
        int "Lua heap limit (KB)"
        default 4096
        range 256 7680
        help
            Total memory one Lua state may hold (PSRAM + internal RAM). Allocations above it
            fail with a Lua "not enough memory" error after an emergency GC, instead of starving
            WiFi / lwIP of RAM.

    config CLU_LUA_INTERNAL_RESERVE_KB
        int "Internal RAM kept free for the system (KB)"
        default 64
        range 16 256
        help
            When PSRAM is full, Lua falls back to internal RAM only while at least this much
            internal RAM stays free.

endmenu
